---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import TripNav from '../../components/TripNav.astro';
import ActivityCard from '../../components/ActivityCard.astro';
import { tripBySlug } from '../../data/trips.ts';
import { groupedFor } from '../../data/activities.ts';
import { durationDays } from '../../lib/trips.ts';

const trip = tripBySlug('vegas');
const groups = groupedFor('vegas');
const nights = durationDays(trip) - 1;

const sections = groups.map((g) => ({ href: `#${g.id}`, label: g.short }));

const who = [
  { name: 'Os', detail: '38' },
  { name: 'Jabari', detail: '30' },
  { name: 'Karen', detail: '64' },
  { name: 'Sa', detail: '50s' },
];

const note =
  `<strong style="color:#E9DCC3">${trip.name} · ${trip.dateLabel}</strong><br>` +
  'Four of us, nine nights, arriving on the 18th and flying home on the 27th.';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={trip.title}
  description={trip.description}
  path={trip.href}
  image={trip.cover}
  ogType="article"
>
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">{trip.name} · {trip.dateLabel}</p>
      <h1>Christmas in Vegas. <em>Help yourself</em>.</h1>
      <p class="lede">{trip.lede}</p>

      <div class="who">
        {
          who.map((p) => (
            <span class="person">
              {p.name}
              <span>{p.detail}</span>
            </span>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <TripNav sections={sections} />

  <section class="shape">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cols">
        <div>
          <h2>The idea</h2>
          <p>
            This is a pile of things that looked fun, not a plan. Nothing is booked and nothing is
            decided. Some of it we might do all together, some in twos, some not at all, and that is
            the whole point of writing it down rather than agreeing an itinerary.
          </p>
          <p>
            Prices are per person unless a card says otherwise, and they are roughly what to expect
            rather than a quote.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="notes">
          <li>
            <b>Doing things apart is fine.</b> Os has work on some of the days, the skydive is not everyone's
            idea of a morning, and Piranha at one in the morning is definitely not. Most of this works
            as a two, and some of it works alone.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>{nights} nights is a long time in Vegas.</b> The Strip wears thin well before the last
            day, which is why about a third of the cards below are an hour or more out of town.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>None of us really gamble.</b> Vdara and the Waldorf Astoria are both at CityCenter, both
            non-gaming and non-smoking, and both do two-bedroom suites, if walking through a lobby instead
            of a slot floor sounds better.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>The rodeo misses us.</b> The National Finals Rodeo runs 3 to 12 December, so it is gone
            before we land. Christmas week is still busy and priced like it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <b>December is properly cold after dark.</b> Highs around 14°C, lows near 4°C. Every outdoor
            thing here wants a coat.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {
    groups.map((group, gi) => (
      <section id={group.id} class:list={['group', { alt: gi % 2 === 1 }]}>
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="head">
            <h2>{group.label}</h2>
            <p>{group.note}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="grid">
            {group.items.map((activity, i) => (
              <ActivityCard activity={activity} eager={gi === 0 && i === 0} />
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    ))
  }

  <section class="book">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>What needs a head start</h2>
      <p class="intro">
        Only relevant for whatever we actually feel like doing. Roughly in the order things stop
        being available.
      </p>
      <ol class="order">
        <li><b>"O"</b><span>Christmas week fills up, and it is dark two nights a week.</span></li>
        <li><b>Helicopter</b><span>Afternoon slots go first, and winter weather cancels.</span></li>
        <li><b>Skydive</b><span>Morning slots are the calm ones and the popular ones.</span></li>
        <li>
          <b>Battlefield Vegas</b><span>
            Worth a phone call rather than a web booking, since only the two-person package is
            published.</span
          >
        </li>
        <li><b>Omega Mart, Neon Museum</b><span>Both timed entry, and dusk goes first.</span></li>
        <li><b>A car</b><span>Needed for anything in the out-of-town section.</span></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="caveat">
        Prices and schedules here were checked in August 2026 and none of it is booked. Worth
        confirming before anyone plans a day around it, especially on 24 and 25 December, when
        opening hours across the city move.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SiteFooter credits={trip.credits} note={note} />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 60px 0 40px;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    max-width: 15ch;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 8.4vw, 92px);
  }

  .hero h1 em {
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--chili);
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 48ch;
    margin-top: 22px;
    font-size: clamp(17px, 2.1vw, 20px);
    opacity: 0.86;
  }

  .who {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }

  .person {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 5px 13px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(26, 18, 13, 0.24);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .person span {
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  section {
    padding: 62px 0;
  }

  .shape {
    padding-top: 54px;
  }

  .cols {
    display: grid;
    gap: 30px;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .cols h2 {
    font-size: clamp(24px, 3.4vw, 30px);
  }

  .cols p {
    margin-top: 14px;
    max-width: 46ch;
    opacity: 0.86;
  }

  .notes {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .notes li {
    padding-left: 16px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--marigold);
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    opacity: 0.9;
  }

  .notes b {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .group.alt {
    background: rgba(26, 18, 13, 0.035);
  }

  .head {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 6px 18px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    padding-bottom: 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .head h2 {
    font-size: clamp(26px, 4vw, 36px);
  }

  .head p {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    opacity: 0.58;
  }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 18px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(290px, 1fr));
  }

  .book {
    background: var(--abyss);
    color: var(--foam);
  }

  .book h2 {
    font-size: clamp(26px, 4vw, 36px);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .order {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
  }

  .order li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 34px minmax(0, 12ch) 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 14px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(214, 231, 227, 0.16);
    counter-increment: step;
  }

  .order li::before {
    content: '0' counter(step);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    opacity: 0.45;
  }

  .order b {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .order span {
    font-size: 15px;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  .intro {
    max-width: 54ch;
    margin: -10px 0 26px;
    opacity: 0.78;
  }

  .caveat {
    margin: 26px 0 0;
    padding-top: 18px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(214, 231, 227, 0.16);
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.15fr;
      gap: 54px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .hero {
      padding: 40px 0 30px;
    }

    section {
      padding: 46px 0;
    }

    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .head {
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    /* Stack the step number above the label so long text keeps its width. */
    .order li {
      grid-template-columns: 26px 1fr;
      gap: 4px 12px;
      padding: 16px 0;
    }

    .order b {
      grid-column: 2;
    }

    .order span {
      grid-column: 2;
    }
  }
</style>
